  "text": " \n                 APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 9 Chapter 232\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8884-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the public health law and the state finance law, in\n        relation  to  enacting  the Lorena Borjas transgender and gender\n        non-binary (TGNB) wellness and equity fund\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This legislation enacts the Lorena Borjas Transgender  and  Non-Binary\nWellness  and  Equity Program Fund, under the administration of the AIDS\nInstitute at the Department of Health for the purpose of funding grants,\nupon appropriation, to organizations serving  people  that  identify  as\ntransgender, gender nonconforming, non-binary and intersex.\n \n  I  fully support this legislation. At a time when the rights of trans-\ngender, gender nonconforming and non-binary people are under  attack  in\nother states, New York is making bold, transformative and nation-leading\ninvestments to support this community.\n \n  This  bill  needed  technical and grammatical edits to ensure that the\nlegislation had the most appropriate language for the community.   Addi-\ntionally, since this legislation was passed outside of the state's budg-\net  process,  the  Legislature  has agreed to move the effective date of\nimplementation of this legislation to April 1, 2023.\n \n  With these changes, I am pleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2022
 },
